WEBVTT

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.470
<i>Our next story is a report regarding</i>
<i>LIVE Corporation chairman</i>

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.890
<i>Steven Martland's abduction.</i>

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.100
-Eve, you're here.
<i>-Last night,</i>

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.730
<i>-the police had a rescue operation</i>
-Good morning! Did I wake you?

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.980
-No. Sorry about yesterday. Our promise...
<i>-and arrested all criminals at the scene.</i>

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.910
-It's fine, I'm used to it. You have work.
<i>-Martland was safely taken to a hospital.</i>

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.160
The news has been running this story
all morning.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:47.000
<i>A press conference was held earlier</i>
<i>at LIVE Corporation headquarters.</i>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>The police are currently questioning</i>
<i>the criminal organization.</i>

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.390
<i>However, they have yet to find</i>
<i>a connection with our firm,</i>

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.430
<i>and believe they targeted</i>
<i>Mr. Martland independently.</i>

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.430
<i>That was the press--</i>

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.310
I have the day off today.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.150
Let me make it up to you.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.400
Really?

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.400
I'll be done with work early today,
so how about having lunch together?

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.990
Okay, I'll come pick you up.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.420
What?

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.210
Nothing!

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.420
Come on.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.750
I mean,
I haven't seen your face in a while.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.640
Did you gain weight?

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.640
Just because you never gain weight!

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.560
Sorry, it was just a joke!

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.980
You and your pretty face!

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.240
So, then Monica yelled at me saying:

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.490
"You have to keep an eye on James!"

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.120
Like it was my fault.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.880
His recklessness is always
getting us into trouble...

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.970
but it usually turns out for the best.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.890
Shouldn't you get that?

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:27.640
Speak of the devil.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:28.770
It's James.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.150
I told him I was taking the day off.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.150
Your face lights up
whenever you're talking about James.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.160
Give me a break, will you?

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.570
Harry.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:43.370
Hold on.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.620
Don't move.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.660
Ouch!

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.370
What was that for?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.050
Just so you know,

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.920
women get jealous even when you're talking
about another man.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.550
It could be a case.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:03.930
You should go.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:05.930
Eve.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.350
Sorry, Eve. Thanks.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.060
Are you apologizing

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.900
or are you thanking me?

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:19.780
I'll be back.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.330
What made you want to look
through these pictures?

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:14.960
My photographer friend
said he'd make large prints for me.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.960
Not that one!

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.510
Stop being so embarrassed.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.800
Oh, this was our two-year anniversary.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:28.970
That takes me back.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.220
Wait, how many years has it been?

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.600
Are you serious?

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.350
I'm just kidding.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.940
You know...

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:43.610
What?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.870
There's something I want to talk about
once things settle down a bit.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.210
Me, too.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.840
There's something I have to tell you.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.080
Could you pull over here?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.500
Harry Creighton.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.600
Sorry to stop you like this.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.270
You're Harry Creighton from the SSC?

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.980
I'm Geffrey Connor
with the LIVE Corporation.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.280
I can't thank you enough for what you did
for our chairman's case.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.280
I was just doing my job.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.990
I'm surprised to see someone as talented
as you with the police.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.710
I'm in the process of creating
a new department.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.210
If you're interested,
I'd like you to head it.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.590
Work for a shady military company?

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.340
You must be joking.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.220
No, I'm dead serious.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:32.940
There's no mistake.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.360
Are you being serious?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.820
I know what it sounds like.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.620
But Grimm suddenly aged rapidly.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.670
We can talk more about that here.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.960
Make sure to arrange the body's transport.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.010
-Copy that.
<i>-And let me talk to Sarah.</i>

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.260
Sarah speaking.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:07.270
I'm really glad you're okay.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:12.730
I'm sorry.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:16.280
<i>Sarah, I understand how you feel...</i>

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.360
but don't be so reckless in the future.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.620
I want you to come back here with James.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.870
I'd like to hear your account, too.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:36.800
Understood.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.050
Sarah.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.350
I'm not sure how to put it...

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:48.140
but...

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:50.770
I know exactly...

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:53.360
what you're feeling.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.440
Sorry.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.550
I hear the culprit
hasn't been identified yet.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.680
Yes, about that...

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:28.220
There are reports
that the attacker was Grimm.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.480
-Grimm? The serial killer?
-Yes.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.690
He died in prison.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.150
I know what you're thinking.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.450
Are you serious?

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.410
He's being transported now.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.830
We are continuing to analyze the video...

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.250
but we don't have an answer yet.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.580
However, if we studied the body...

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.960
The body? You let him die?

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:59.840
You lot at the SSC
always do whatever you like.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:03.550
It was unavoidable.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.770
<i>There's been a strict gag order</i>
<i>regarding this incident.</i>

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.650
<i>I understand.</i>

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:17.900
<i>We can't very well announce that a police</i>
<i>organization has been openly attacked.</i>

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:23.400
And we can't bring in
this nonsense either.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.160
You're telling me to take care
of the body secretly?

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.910
I'm telling you
to avoid causing confusion.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.250
And the body isn't necessarily Grimm.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.380
And if it is?

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.820
What is this Mask?

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.200
Did Monica find out what they were...?

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:11.950
And was killed for it.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:35.270
There are too many discrepancies
regarding the attacker's footage.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:39.400
There isn't much meaning
to the analysis right now...

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.480
but this caught my attention.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.860
Eddy, do you have a second?

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:53.660
Grimm's unbelievable ability
and his abnormal death.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.500
This isn't some ordinary Mask.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:01.630
Nobody is going to listen...

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.210
about this Mask right now.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:08.300
That's why we need to look into it
at the SSC.

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.010
If we analyze the Mask,

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.220
we'll be able to find out the truth...

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.020
behind Grimm's case and Monica's death.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:18.520
I'm sure of it.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.360
James is saying

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.740
that the attacker was Grimm.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.030
What?

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:31.990
Sarah was there,
and she's saying the same thing.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:37.080
We were talking about that in the
conference room when you walked in.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.040
Wait, but...

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:44.250
You know full well that James isn't
the kind of guy to joke about that.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:47.470
But he died in prison.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:51.260
What if Grimm never died?

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.220
Is that possible?

00:14:58.430 --> 00:14:59.270
I don't know.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:03.730
The three years since James caught him...

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.440
Do you think you can find out
what he's been doing?

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.160
I'll try.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:18.910
The dead came back just to die again,
and now we're looking into it.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.250
It's like playing along with a bad joke.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.550
But that's our only option right now.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.260
But...

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:34.300
what was he trying to do?

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:38.770
If he somehow managed to escape
prison after James arrested him,

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.310
then why would he do something
so dangerous?

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.770
What if the answer is simple?

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.690
What if he just wanted to see James?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.200
No way.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.870
Anyway, I'll look into his whereabouts
these past three years.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.670
And I'll look into the Mask.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.380
Continue along the route--

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:57.260
Can you hear me?

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:01.310
What's going on?

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:07.650
-Do it now!
-What's going on?

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.650
-Try switching to another line.
-I'm trying!

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.150
This night never ends!

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.170
I can't get through.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:30.250
-What's going on?
-I don't know.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.210
<i>We lost contact with HQ, too.</i>

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:35.840
I can't restore a connection to transport.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:37.840
Considering our situation,

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:40.350
it's hard to imagine
it's just communication failure.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:41.760
I agree.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.180
Eddy, what about the highway cameras?

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.730
I'll pull them up.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:49.400
They're out.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.440
We're completely cut off.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.200
I should take charge here.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:29.900
Sarah, stay down!

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:24.080
Hold on tight.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.110
Sarah. Are you okay?

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.690
Sarah! Sarah!

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:43.570
Sarah!

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.890
Grimm and Number Nine have been recovered.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:14.940
Was it Harry?

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:16.310
Yes.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:17.350
Impressive.

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:18.900
Yes.

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:26.280
Yes, she's unconscious right now,

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.660
but nothing life threatening.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.330
Yes, I'm fine.

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:34.410
It's just... the Mask and Grimm's body...

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:36.830
were both taken.

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:43.920
How many Masks remain?

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:48.300
Only one.

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:53.350
The police are making moves.

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:56.140
I don't want any more trouble.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:58.730
Yes, sir.

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:37.020
<i>Connecting to voice mail.</i>

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:49.610
May...

00:24:19.290 --> 00:24:21.790
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
